WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.219
I'm about to sign into law

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.989
bipartisan safety measures, gun

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:05.309
safety legislation.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.499
And time is of the essence.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.759
Lives will be saved.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.709
When it seems impossible to get

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.839
anything done in Washington, we are

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.729
doing something consequential.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.369
We can reach compromise on guns.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.269
We ought to be able to reach

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:20.829
compromise on other critical issues.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.869
The new gun law is not an inspiring

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.699
example of bipartisan cooperation

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.439
to protect public safety.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.789
It's an illustration of how the

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:29.439
worst instincts of both major

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.569
parties combine to produce policies

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.699
that are neither just nor sensible.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.929
The bill passed the Senate by

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.489
unanimous consent and passed the

00:00:36.490 --> 00:00:38.109
House with bipartisan support

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:39.549
because it offered something to both

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.329
sides.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.069
Republicans got tougher sentences,

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:44.019
Democrats got more gun control, and

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.429
both got to pretend they were doing

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:47.289
something to prevent mass shootings.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:48.519
The law is unlikely to have a

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.319
meaningful impact on mass shootings,

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.999
but it will cancel the gun rights of

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.039
adults based on juvenile records and

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.839
subsidize state laws that suspend

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.519
those rights without due process.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.049
It also increases the maximum

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:00.879
penalty for gun possession by people

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.749
with felony records from 10 to

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.609
15 years.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.439
That ban applies no matter how old

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.269
the conviction is and regardless of

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:08.499
whether the offense involved

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.279
violence.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:10.899
The law created additional criminal

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.729
penalties of up to 15 years in

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.099
prison for trafficking in firearms,

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.749
which is defined so broadly that it

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:18.309
covers any prohibited person who

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.179
receives a gun.

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:20.739
Prohibited persons who are legally

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:22.539
disqualified from owning firearms

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.009
include millions of Americans with

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.629
no history of violence such as

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:26.979
cannabis consumers, former

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.569
psychiatric patients who have never

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:30.069
been deemed a threat to others, and

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:31.659
people convicted of drug crimes or

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:33.219
other nonviolent felonies.

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.719
Thanks to this law, a cannabis

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.309
consumer could go to prison for up

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.199
to 15 years if he obtains a

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.239
gun, even if he lives in a state

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:41.769
that has legalized marijuana.

00:01:41.770 --> 00:01:43.239
That trafficking and firearms

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.979
penalty also applies to people who

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:46.449
have lost the right to own guns

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.009
under state law, even when they are

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:49.929
not disqualified under federal law.

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.069
These new penalties will

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:52.389
disproportionately harm

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:53.649
African-Americans.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.509
Last fiscal year, 89%

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:57.429
of federal firearms offenses involve

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.499
illegal possession, often without

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.119
aggravating circumstances or a

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.199
history of violence.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.089
55% of those defendants

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:05.949
were black. Even the American Civil

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.389
Liberties Union, which thinks the

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:08.769
right to keep and bear arms is a

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.029
figment of the Supreme Court's

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.889
imagination, recognizes that

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.179
the categories of people that

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.859
federal law currently prohibits from

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.659
possessing or purchasing a gun are

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:18.519
overbroad and not reasonably

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:20.199
related to the state's interest in

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.159
public safety.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.199
The ACLU says those gun bans

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.029
raise significant equal protection

00:02:25.030 --> 00:02:26.769
and due process concerns.

00:02:26.770 --> 00:02:28.689
As an appeals court judge, Supreme

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.699
Court Justice Amy Coney Barrett went

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.079
even further, arguing that the

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.969
wildly over inclusive gun ban

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:35.439
for people with felony records

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.939
violates the Second Amendment.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.559
Undeterred by such criticism,

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.089
Republicans who claim to support the

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.799
Second Amendment voted not only to

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.239
continue punishing people for

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:45.099
exercising the rights it guarantees,

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.569
but to increase the penalties they

00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:48.789
face. So did Democrats, despite

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:50.019
their avowed concern about

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.939
excessively severe sentences, racial

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.769
disparities and the damage done

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.119
by the war on drugs.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.099
This is what bipartisan compromise

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.539
means in Washington; I will

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.429
compromise my principles if you

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.430
compromise yours.

